rnet telephones  mobile phones etc they have been able to  navigate many many technology  innovations and evolutions so people  like that who continue to reinvent  themselves who continue to incorporate  new technologies and become successful  they are likely to actually do pretty  well here it's in the dna of what they  do is to use new technology but there's  plenty of old school firms whether it's  because the leadership team is out of  touch with technology or their dna is  just the last mover those are the people  who are most susceptible because it's  one thing when the internet comes around  or when mobile phones come around those  are technologies that could help you do  your job but they're not directly a  replacement for your services they may  help you do a better job but they don't  necessarily replace what you do this is  different if all of a sudden you're  talking about hey we're in the lending  business but there's a decentralized  lending opportunity that ends up being a  zero-sum game to some degree so what i  think we're going to watch happen is  that there's going to be a contrarian  idea today eventually become a consensus  idea which is these banks are going to  continue to push further and further and  further into the industry and they're  going to embrace this new technology  because they're going to have to now  many of them are waiting because they  need this guidance they need to have  their compliance officers their lawyers  and their regulators give them the green  light if the occ the federal reserve and  the fdic come out and say listen we give  you the green light within these  parameters within this box go do these  activities as long as you do these  activities you're good  expect every single bank or financial  institution to immediately run to that  area so in some way when the regulators  and the lawyers and the compliance  departments and fdic  federal reserve occ etc come out with  this guidance they essentially are going  to 